# Component file structure

Two layouts. **Do not mix them up.**

## A) Shared kit — `src/components/{elements,form,ui}/`

Reuse across features. **One folder per component** (kebab-case):

```
my-foo/
  my-foo.tsx
  index.ts       # re-export only — never implement here
  type.ts        # all props / exported types
  styles.ts      # generateStyles(theme)
  hooks.ts       # optional
```

Product-only wrappers next to a kit (e.g. `private-sidebar.tsx`) may use `private-sidebar.styles.ts` instead of bloating the shared kit `styles.ts`.

## B) Feature-only UI — `src/features/<feature>/components/`

Presentational pieces used **only** by that feature.

**Flat folder — no per-component subfolders:**

```
src/features/<feature>/components/
  styles.ts              # shared generateStyles for all feature components
  type.ts                # shared props / component types
  order-summary-card.tsx # 1 file = 1 component
  status-badge.tsx
  …
```

Rules:

- **Do not** put feature-only UI under `src/components/ui`.
- **Do not** create `order-summary-card/index.ts` + `styles.ts` + `type.ts` trees inside the feature.
- Prefer shared `components/styles.ts` (or screen `styles.ts`) over one styles file per component.
- Keep production screens thin: `screens/` = container + view + screen styles; extract large JSX into `components/*.tsx`.

Screen standard: `container.tsx` + `view.tsx` + `styles.ts` under `features/<feature>/screens/` — see `.docs/screen-standard.md`.
